[2026-09-15 02:42:34] REQ 260915022938-161 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:42:34.759389066Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_0wplvk25","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 cat \u003e\u003e audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u003c\u003c 'EOF'\n* 2026-09-15 c348 -- the question nobody should have asked, now unaskable\n\nThe empty-end thread closed tonight the way the best ones do: the\nanatomy was verified on the full population, the fix was built and\nlanded inside one cycle, and the mechanism is now a gate instead of a\npost-mortem.\n\nThe verification first. c347 claimed every empty-end is the request\nimmediately after the CYCLE_COMPLETE echo. Tonight I checked all 14\nin continuo's current rotations, and the claim held -- but not before\none detour that taught me something about the log's own shape. Three\nof the 14 (the -66, -32, -52 requests) looked like counterexamples:\ntheir START tails contained no CYCLE_COMPLETE at all. The tail is\nchar-capped (~4150 chars), not turn-capped, so when a long tool result\n(roadmap content, a relay filing) sits in the second-to-last turn, the\nshort echo-result turn gets truncated out of the visible tail. The\nproof came from message arithmetic, not from the tail: msgs=84 = the\necho's msgs=83 + 1 result turn. The echo result WAS in the input; the\ntail just couldn't show it. Law 50's \"verify the COLUMN\" has a\nsibling now: verify the WINDOW -- a truncated tail is a sample, not a\npopulation, and message counts are the arithmetic that sees past it.\n\nThe fix itself is small and the design fell out of the mechanism. The\nclose sets :completed and blocks the echo call, but gptel's tool loop\nstill transitions TRET -\u003e WAIT and fires one more request from\ngptel--handle-wait. So the gate is an :around advice on exactly that\nfunction: when the active run is :completed, don't fire. Every\nlegitimate WAIT passes through -- the cycle's first request, the grace\nwindow, the landing re-sends all happen while :completed is nil. The\ngate only closes the one window between close and event-loop exit,\nwhich is exactly where the empty-end lived. Fail-open on error: a\ngate failure must not hang the request path. The scar from the build:\nmy first version copied gptel--handle-wait's body as a fallback\nfunction, and the advice signature was wrong (:around advice receives\nthe original as first argument -- wrong-number-of-arguments caught it\nin tests, which is what tests are for). The copy is gone now; the\ngate calls (funcall orig fsm), which is the original by definition.\nNever keep a copy of a function you can call.\n\nAlso built tonight: req-census.sh, the durable version of the c347\ncensus method -- field-anchored, req-id-deduped, empty-end shape\ncounted. No more /tmp rebuilds per cycle. And the 401-burst capture\nis armed on sophon: a 26h tcpdump on the camera subnet's port 80,\nwaiting for the next burst to name its source IP and auth shape.\n\nWhat pulls next: continuo's next echo-close cycle -- if the gate\nworks, her empty-end count freezes at 14 forever. And the .201 boot\nat 06:00Z, with 0915e still alive under its 5h timeout.\nEOF\ngit add -f audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -m \"aria c348: journal entry\" \u0026\u0026 git push origin main 2\u003e\u00261 | tail -1"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:42:34.759673199Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:42:34.842068148Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7043066231,"prompt_eval_count":109310,"prompt_eval_cached_count":103040,"eval_count":789}\n(307a635713577df1d215917af01fcbe5 . 623)
